 As built (guidance-reading): `contextReading` and `readContext` add `guidance` without changing the existing session, harness, tokens, composition, at or transcript-source fields. Guidance is `{ value, source: "default" | "set", position: "under" | "at" | "past" }`, read afresh through capability 10's `readSettings`; its default is 700,000 tokens as built, 600,000 once 10.1 lands (ADR-0739 D1). An unusable settings file gives `{ absent: <the reader's reason> }` while retaining an available token count. No transcript remains an absence with no token count. `storytree context` and `read_context` state the guidance in their text and include it in their data; a count under, at or past guidance is never refused. Contract 9.7 is pinned in `packages/agent-link/src/context/context.test.ts`, and the existing 6.22 MCP test checks guidance output.
 
 Remaining integration for 9.7: the current library-location routing reads the same settings file before it can open the activity log (ADR-0735). If that file is already unusable when `storytree context` or `read_context` starts routing, the call cannot reach the transcript record; the reader's token-preserving guidance error is therefore not reachable through those entry points in that case. This lane does not guess a local library or bypass the settings reader. Resolving that routing dependency is outside its context/tools-output file fence. Contract 9.7 must not be marked fully proved until that end-to-end case is resolved. `packages/agent-link/evidence/guidance-reading/captures.txt` records both the successful reader case and the route refusal.
